{
  "reading": "Study 015: which card leaves jaws-v1 so Irencrag Pyromancer comes in. The pilot's premise is too many wheels and too few permanents. Four wheels were screened, and Time Reversal is the cheapest one to lose: it has the smallest damage loss of the three pure wheels, it shuffles away the graveyard Conspiracy Theorist recurs from, and it costs five mana. Collective Defiance shows the smallest damage loss, but its removal and burn modes overlap Pyromancer's job.",
  "log_entries_read": ["006"],
  "cut_candidates": [
    {"card": "Time Reversal", "why": "A 5-mana wheel that shuffles both graveyards into the libraries, so Theorist and flashback have nothing to work with. Goldfish (one instrument): damage @T10 -8.7 [-10.2,-7.3]; finisher wheel by T8 -3.0 pts [-3.4,-2.7]; cards handed to each opponent by T8 -0.75 (better).", "cost_of_cutting": "One of the deck's 7+ draw-sevens is gone. That means fewer Shabraz counters and Brallin discards, and wheels cast by T10 drops 2.90 -> 2.69.", "difficulty": "contested", "orphans_stack": []},
    {"card": "Reforge the Soul", "why": "Five mana outside a miracle turn, and the deck has few ways to set one up. Goldfish: damage @T10 -10.4 [-11.9,-9.0]; finisher wheel -3.0 pts.", "cost_of_cutting": "A second draw-seven goes. Its damage cost is close to Windfall's, which has verified stacks 001 and 002 and stays.", "difficulty": "painful", "orphans_stack": []}
  ],
  "add_candidates": [{"card": "Irencrag Pyromancer", "closes": "interaction", "source": "prompt", "why": "A 3-mana permanent that deals 3 to any target on each second draw. It is repeatable removal and reach, and the goldfish cannot see its removal.", "natural_cut": "Time Reversal"}],
  "open_questions": [],
  "gaps": ["The goldfish reads Pyromancer's face damage only. Its creature removal is unread, so every row undercounts it.", "Torbran still appears in the try neighbour list but is not on the branch, so that index is stale."]
